# Read by `vite build` (the Docker web image, CI and any static host), never by `npm run dev`.
# A production build serves the database through the API for every role. Nothing here is a secret.
# VITE_DATA_SOURCE: live = every role on the database; mock (or unset) = every role on the in-browser mocks.
VITE_DATA_SOURCE=live
# Local development keeps the mocks unless you set these in the shell or in frontend/.env.local.
# VITE_API_BASE is left unset on purpose: the app then calls its own origin, and nginx (deploy/web/nginx.conf) proxies /api.
# A static host with no /api proxy (Cloudflare Pages or Workers assets) must set VITE_API_BASE at build time to the API's
# origin, with no trailing slash, and add the site's origin to the API's CORS_ORIGINS.
